   Estudios Agua, CICY},
Abstract = {The purpose of this paper is review the information of the species
   belonging. to seven holoplanktonic families of polychaetes: Alciopidae,
   lospilidae, Lopadorhynchidae, Pontodoridae, Tomopteridae,
   Typhloscolecidae. and Yndolaciidae. The Survey region is the Atlantic
   Ocean arbitrary considerate between 60 degrees N to 60 degrees S, and 97
   degrees W to 20 degrees E. Seventy one species have been recorded which
   diversity patterns are analyzed, including particular data front the
   eastern and western regions as the Canarian Archipelago and Cabo Verde
   Islands, and the Yucatan Channel (between Gulf of Mexico and Caribbean
   Sea). respectively. Zoogeographic affinities and faunistic composition
   differences are discussed.},
