Abstract = {The height of the aquaculture of shrimp, the high demand of the product,
   the overexplolation of wild larvae, the loss of life, the propensity to
   diseases and the little resistance of the larvae of natural mean's,
   impelled the development of investigations of reproduction of shrimps
   for the obtaining of larvae by means of egg-layings in laboratory to
   replace the capture of cultivated wild organisms by, assuring one better
   quality these, which originated the sprouting of the culture of larvae
   of shrimp known like larviculture. In monitoring the shrimp to detect
   mortality factors, slow growth or aspects during its cultivation farms
   and laboratories. Is very important physico-chemical studies on
   environmental, microbiological and physiological; Within the latter are
   the histological studies that allow Lis to know the normal structure of
   each larval stage until it reaches the adult and be able to determine
   the damage caused by various pathogens that affect them.},
