Volume = {22},
Number = {1},
Pages = {103-116},
Month = {JAN-MAR},
Abstract = {Sample sites was distributed on the Santiago river before, in and after
   of the Aguamilpa Dam construction between 1992 and 1997. The objetive
   was the detection of the impacts on the plankton community with the
   application of the Water Quality Index (WCI), Secuential Comparison
   Index (SCI), the Shannon-Weiner Index (H') and the Saprobiological Index
   (S) on the phytoplanctonic community. The physicochemical water quality
   was interpreted with de Ecological Criteria for the Aquatic Life
   Protection in the Freshwater and Coastal Water of Mexico. The results
   showed organic contamination in the water column, where Scenedesmus,
   Oscillatoria y Alaucoseira crenulata was the bioindicators in these
   environmental conditions. The dam showed eutrophic tendence due at the
   nutrients (N). The phytoplankton community doesn't change.},
