Year = {2006},
Number = {1259},
Pages = {61-68},
Month = {JUL 14},
Abstract = {This is the first record of the genus Simognathus and of the subfamily
   Simognathinae from Mexico. Simognathus cramerae sp. nov. is described
   from the Mexican tropical Pacific Ocean. The principal diagnostic
   features are dorsal setae 2 outside of ocular plate, dorsal setae 3 on
   anterodorsal plate, and second segment of pedipalp with a ventral
   bristle and without a ventral apophysis. This species resembles S.
   fuscus Viets, S. similis Bartsch, and S. hulingsi Newell.},
