Abstract = {A new species of Thoreauea J. K. Williams is proposed. This species
   differs from Thoreauea paneroi J. K. Williams in its corolline crown
   10-lobulate at the apex and stamens as long as the crown. The species
   described in this paper was found in habitats of forests of Pinus L.,
   Quercus L., and Abies Miller and in montane rain forest found in the
   highest region of the Sierra of Guerrero. The fruits and seeds are
   described for the first time for this genus.},
