   Soc; Natl Council Sci \& Technol; Latin Amer Phys Ctr; Int Atom Energy
   Agcy},
Abstract = {This article deals with the measurement of the mobility of negative ions
   in the mixtures of CCl4 with Ar with the CCl4 ratio up to 33.3\%. The
   Pulsed Townsend Technique was employed to produce an integrated ionic
   avalanches over a range of the density-reduced electric field E/N for
   which ionization is either negligible or absent, and attachment
   processes are dominant leading to the formation of mostly CCl4-. The E/N
   range of measurement was I to 50 Td (1Td = 10(-17) Vcm(2)). Our
   measurements strongly suggest that attachment is the dominant process
   and only negative ions are formed.},
