Abstract = {We investigated the electronic structure of three recently discovered
   Zintl-phase hydrides: SrAl2H2, Ca3SnH2, and Ca5Sn3H. The energy bands
   and the total and partial densities of states were computed by means of
   the full-potential linearized augmented-plane-wave method. We found the
   SrAl2H2 and Ca5Sn3H hydrides are metallic and Ca3SnH2 is a small-gap
   semiconductor. We analyzed the chemical bonding features of this series
   of compounds. (C) 2004 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.},
