   2005), Monterrey, MEXICO, NOV 14-18, 2005},
Abstract = {The objective of this work is to automatically determine, in an
   unsupervised manner, Spanish prepositional phrases of the type
   preposition - nominal phrase - preposition (P-NP-P) that behave in a
   sentence as a lexical unit and their semantic and syntactic properties
   cannot be deduced from the corresponding properties of each simple form,
   e.g., por medio de (by means of), a fin de (in order to), con respecto a
   (with respect to). We show that idiomatic P-NP-P combinations have some
   statistical properties distinct from those of usual idiomatic
   collocations. We also explore a way to differentiate P-NP-P combinations
   that could perform either as a regular prepositional phrase or as
   idiomatic prepositional phrase.},
