Title = {Useful wild fungi of La Malinche National Park, Mexico},
Journal = {FUNGAL DIVERSITY},
Year = {2004},
Volume = {17},
Pages = {115-143},
Month = {OCT 1},
Abstract = {This study presents a list of 93 fungi species collected from La
   Malinche National Park, Tlaxcala, Mexico. The fungi were gathered mainly
   during the rainy seasons of 1988-2002. Of the species identified, 10
   were Ascomycota, 82 Basidiomycota and one Myxomycota. This study
   provides information about the habitat, phenology and life forms of the
   species studied. Further-more, an ethnobiological technique known as
   free listing was used to identify the most important species of fungi
   for 84 people. living on the volcano called La Malinche. Boletus
   pinophilus was the species the respondents mentioned most frequently. No
   differences were observed between males and females in terms of the
   fungi they were familiar with. There were, however, some differences in
   the species mentioned by the people of Javier Mina and San Isidro
   Buensuceso, two towns on the slopes of La Malinche.},
